   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a8e9af91",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Classifier Comparison: Understanding Decision Boundaries\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook compares 10 scikit-learn classifiers on three synthetic datasets. Each row represents a dataset; the first column shows the input data, and the remaining columns show each classifier's decision boundary and test accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Learning goal:** understand how different algorithms separate classes in 2D. These synthetic results should not be treated as proof of real-world performance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "979337d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Import the Required Libraries\n",
    "**Purpose:** Import plotting tools, dataset generators, model classes, preprocessing, and decision-boundary visualization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "164e62ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from matplotlib.colors import ListedColormap\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.base import clone\n",
    "from sklearn.datasets import make_circles, make_classification, make_moons\n",
    "from sklearn.discriminant_analysis import QuadraticDiscriminantAnalysis\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import AdaBoostClassifier, RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.gaussian_process import GaussianProcessClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.gaussian_process.kernels import RBF\n",
    "from sklearn.inspection import DecisionBoundaryDisplay\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.naive_bayes import GaussianNB\n",
    "from sklearn.neighbors import KNeighborsClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.neural_network import MLPClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.svm import SVC\n",
    "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    accuracy_score,\n",
    "    classification_report,\n",
    "    ConfusionMatrixDisplay,\n",
    "    confusion_matrix,\n",
    "    f1_score,\n",
    "    precision_score,\n",
    "    recall_score,\n",
    ")\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold, cross_val_score, GridSearchCV\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "465b2fb4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Define the Classifiers\n",
    "**Purpose:** Set up the 10 classification algorithms and their parameters. `names` provides the matching plot titles."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "12da41fc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "names = [\n",
    "    \"Nearest Neighbors\", \"Linear SVM\", \"RBF SVM\", \"Gaussian Process\",\n",
    "    \"Decision Tree\", \"Random Forest\", \"Neural Net\", \"AdaBoost\",\n",
    "    \"Naive Bayes\", \"QDA\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "classifiers = [\n",
    "    KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=3),\n",
    "    SVC(kernel=\"linear\", C=0.025, random_state=42),\n",
    "    SVC(gamma=2, C=1, random_state=42),\n",
    "    GaussianProcessClassifier(1.0 * RBF(1.0), random_state=42),\n",
    "    DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=5, random_state=42),\n",
    "    RandomForestClassifier(\n",
    "        max_depth=5, n_estimators=10, max_features=1, random_state=42\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    MLPClassifier(alpha=1, max_iter=1000, random_state=42),\n",
    "    AdaBoostClassifier(random_state=42),\n",
    "    GaussianNB(),\n",
    "    QuadraticDiscriminantAnalysis(),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "assert len(names) == len(classifiers), \"Each classifier must have a display name.\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d83a452d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Create the Synthetic Datasets\n",
    "**Purpose:** Generate three 2D datasets with different shapes:\n",
    "- `make_moons`: crescent-shaped classes.\n",
    "- `make_circles`: inner and outer circles.\n",
    "- `make_classification`: a generated binary classification dataset with two informative features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "496a0196",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X, y = make_classification(\n",
    "    n_features=2,\n",
    "    n_redundant=0,\n",
    "    n_informative=2,\n",
    "    random_state=1,\n",
    "    n_clusters_per_class=1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "rng = np.random.RandomState(2)\n",
    "X = X + 2 * rng.uniform(size=X.shape)\n",
    "linearly_separable = (X, y)\n",
    "\n",
    "datasets = [\n",
    "    make_moons(noise=0.3, random_state=0),\n",
    "    make_circles(noise=0.2, factor=0.5, random_state=1),\n",
    "    linearly_separable,\n",
    "]\n",
    "dataset_names = [\"Moons\", \"Circles\", \"Classification Data\"]\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "64cb9c2f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Create the Plot Grid and Compare Models\n",
    "**Purpose:** Build a grid with three rows and eleven columns. For each dataset, split the data into training and test sets, plot the original points, fit each classifier inside a scaling pipeline, calculate test accuracy, and display its decision boundary.\n",
    "\n",
   
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "444f4563",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 2700x900 with 33 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(\n",
    "    nrows=len(datasets),\n",
    "    ncols=len(classifiers) + 1,\n",
    "    figsize=(27, 9),\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "class_colors = ListedColormap([\"#FF0000\", \"#0000FF\"])\n",
    "boundary_cmap = plt.cm.RdBu\n",
    "\n",
    "for row_index, (dataset_name, dataset) in enumerate(zip(dataset_names, datasets)):\n",
    "    X, y = dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "    X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "        X, y, test_size=0.4, random_state=42\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    x_min, x_max = X[:, 0].min() - 0.5, X[:, 0].max() + 0.5\n",
    "    y_min, y_max = X[:, 1].min() - 0.5, X[:, 1].max() + 0.5\n",
    "\n",
    "    # First column: visualize the original dataset.\n",
    "    ax = axes[row_index, 0]\n",
    "    ax.scatter(\n",
    "        X_train[:, 0], X_train[:, 1],\n",
    "        c=y_train, cmap=class_colors, edgecolors=\"k\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    ax.scatter(\n",
    "        X_test[:, 0], X_test[:, 1],\n",
    "        c=y_test, cmap=class_colors, alpha=0.6, edgecolors=\"k\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    ax.set_xlim(x_min, x_max)\n",
    "    ax.set_ylim(y_min, y_max)\n",
    "    ax.set_xticks([])\n",
    "    ax.set_yticks([])\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(dataset_name, fontsize=11)\n",
    "    if row_index == 0:\n",
    "        ax.set_title(\"Input data\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Remaining columns: fit each classifier and draw its decision boundary.\n",
    "    for col_index, (name, classifier) in enumerate(zip(names, classifiers), start=1):\n",
    "        ax = axes[row_index, col_index]\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Scaling is fitted only on training data; clone gives a fresh model per dataset.\n",
    "        model = make_pipeline(StandardScaler(), clone(classifier))\n",
    "        model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "        test_accuracy = model.score(X_test, y_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "        DecisionBoundaryDisplay.from_estimator(\n",
    "            model, X, cmap=boundary_cmap, alpha=0.8, ax=ax, eps=0.5\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "        ax.scatter(\n",
    "            X_train[:, 0], X_train[:, 1],\n",
    "            c=y_train, cmap=class_colors, edgecolors=\"k\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        ax.scatter(\n",
    "            X_test[:, 0], X_test[:, 1],\n",
    "            c=y_test, cmap=class_colors, edgecolors=\"k\", alpha=0.6\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "        ax.set_xlim(x_min, x_max)\n",
    "        ax.set_ylim(y_min, y_max)\n",
    "        ax.set_xticks([])\n",
    "        ax.set_yticks([])\n",
    "\n",
    "        if row_index == 0:\n",
    "            ax.set_title(name, fontsize=9)\n",
    "\n",
    "        ax.text(\n",
    "            0.98, 0.04, f\"{test_accuracy:.2f}\",\n",
    "            transform=ax.transAxes,\n",
    "            size=10,\n",
    "            horizontalalignment=\"right\",\n",
    "            bbox={\"facecolor\": \"white\", \"alpha\": 0.75, \"edgecolor\": \"none\"},\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.suptitle(\"Classifier Comparison on Synthetic Datasets\", fontsize=16, y=1.02)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "465f3231",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Interpret the Results\n",
    "- **Decision boundary:** the colored background indicates the class predicted by the model in each region.\n",
    "- **Training points:** solid markers are used to fit the model.\n",
    "- **Test points:** semi-transparent markers were held out from training.\n",
    "- **Accuracy:** the number in the bottom-right of each classifier panel is its accuracy on the test split.\n",
    "\n",
    "A complicated boundary is not automatically better. Consider test accuracy and whether a model appears to fit the training points too closely.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Notes:** This is a teaching visualization, not a production-model benchmark. Some estimators may issue convergence or numerical warnings depending on the installed library version; inspect the final plots and output to confirm the run completed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9e7623af",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Evaluate Models with Multiple Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose:** Accuracy alone can hide differences between models. This section calculates accuracy, macro precision, macro recall, and macro F1-score on a held-out test set for every classifier and dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why macro averages?** They calculate each class's metric separately and then average the class scores, giving both classes equal weight."
   ]
  },
